&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Insight Enterprises, Inc. is a Fortune 500 Solutions Integrator helping organizations accelerate transformation by unlocking the power of people and technology. We architect, build and manage solutions for complex IT environments to deliver outcomes that contribute to our clients&#39; success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our portfolio of digital transformation services includes deep expertise in cloud, data, AI, cybersecurity and intelligent edge. These services, augmented by Insight&#39;s longstanding relationships with 6,000+ technology partners across the globe, enable us to deliver the right technical solutions quickly and effectively. We&#39;re rated as a Great Place to Work, a Forbes Best Employer for Diversity and a Forbes World&#39;s Top Female-Friendly Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Senior Revenue Operations Manager&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; £62,000 - £80,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Bristol HQ - Hybrid Model (3 days p/w on site)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting into:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Chief Growth Officer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Insight is a global solutions integrator, helping organisations unlock greater value from people, technology and innovation. Insight AI is the specialist AI brand that transforms ideas into measurable business impact through practical, scalable AI solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Revenue Operations Manager, you will play a crucial role in optimising and aligning the processes, technology, and teams across the revenue-generating functions of Insight AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for driving efficiency, scalability, and effectiveness in sales, marketing, and client services operations. This role involves managing the team of Salesforce Administrators and Developers as well as collaborating with various departments to enhance revenue-generating strategies and ensure the seamless integration of systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Accountabilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build rapport, alignment, and operational advocacy among senior management and the executive team;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, design, and implement the processes, programs, and systems to support Insight AI’s revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team management of the Salesforce Administrators and Salesforce Developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop sales operations staff and our marketing team&#39;s into a highly effective machine with deep system expertise;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the training of new and current sales and marketing employees on relevant systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage collection and evaluation of sales &amp;amp; marketing data to improve effectiveness of team and campaigns;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the Marketing Operations function to ensure the seamless transition of MQLs from Marketo, to Salesforce, and reporting back up through Databricks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our Business Intelligence team to take our analysis to the next level, as well as automate reporting;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead roll out of major sales changes such as new pricing;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administrate, monitor adoption, and the ROI of our Sales Tech Stack and make relevant recommendations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve sales and marketing productivity by simplifying processes and evaluating new tools, enabling our team to work smarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engineer processes across CRM and integrations into various other pieces of the tech stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not afraid of being hands on in the CRM, building flows, and automations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in revenue operations, sales operations, or a related role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Salesforce CRM systems, marketing automation tools, and sales processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritise and thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and engineering ETL pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTML, CSS, Javascript, SOQL, SQL experience would be ideal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥 Private medical cover&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🐾 Dog‑friendly Bristol office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍻 In office bar &amp;amp; monthly socials&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚴 Cycle‑to‑work,⚡electric car scheme,🏋️ gym discounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧘 Health &amp;amp; wellbeing apps&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰Discounts for high street brands&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💙 Social &amp;amp; charitable events&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To see more roles, &lt;a href=&quot;https://amdaris.com/jobs&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We love going to work and think you should too. Our team is dedicated to trust, customer obsession, agility, and striving to be better everyday. These values serve as the foundation of our culture, guiding our actions and driving us towards excellence. We foster a culture of performance and recognition, allowing us to transform growth as we enable our employees to do the best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is located in London, England. &lt;/strong&gt;Our office is situated in a core location near Waterloo and Blackfriars on the Southbank. Across the globe, our Centers of Energy serve as hubs where we accelerate productivity and collaboration, inspire creativity, and cultivate a culture of connection and celebration. Our teams coordinate their time in Centers of Energy to reflect how they work best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about life at LogicMonitor, check out our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.logicmonitor.com/careers&quot;&gt;Careers Page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LogicMonitor® is the AI-first hybrid observability platform powering the next generation of digital infrastructure. LogicMonitor delivers complete visibility and actionable intelligence across on-premises, cloud, and edge environments. By anticipating issues before they strike, optimizing resources in real time, and enabling faster, smarter decisions, LogicMonitor helps IT and business leaders protect margins, accelerate innovation, and deliver exceptional digital experiences without compromise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers love LogicMonitor&#39;s ability to bring cloud and traditional IT together into one view, as seen in minimal churn rates, expansion business, and exciting new customer references. In fact, LogicMonitor has received the highest Net Promoter Score of any IT Infrastructure Management provider. LogicMonitor also boasts high employee satisfaction. We have been certified as a Great Place To Work®, and named one of BuiltIn&#39;s Best Places to Work for the seventh year in a row!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Sr. Forward Deployed Engineer who enjoys solving real customer problems through hands-on engineering and AI-driven solutions. In this role, you will work closely with senior engineers, product teams, and customers to design, build, and deploy tailored solutions that extend LogicMonitor Edwin AI. As a Forward deploy Engineer, you will be operating at the intersection of customer delivery and core platform development, with ownership of discovery, scoping, system design, build, rollout, and measurable adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div data-hasbody=&quot;true&quot; data-macro-name=&quot;panel&quot;&gt;
&lt;div data-hasbody=&quot;true&quot; data-macro-name=&quot;panel&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a customer facing engineering role at the intersection of software engineering, observability, and AI deployment. You will ship code, implement integrations, support production rollouts, and codify repeatable patterns that improve both customer outcomes and the core platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s a closer look at this key role:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Support AI-Powered Solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with strategic customers to build production applications, ship technical artifacts used in production workflows, codify repeatable deployment patterns, and represent the company in highly ambiguous enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineers and customers to understand use cases, workflows, and technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain backend services, integrations, automations, and lightweight full stack experiences using Python and JavaScript or TypeScript.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement REST API, webhook, and SDK based integrations that normalize, enrich, and route operational data into LogicMonitor Edwin AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument and troubleshoot telemetry across logs, metrics, traces, and related workflow data, including OpenTelemetry based pipelines where appropriate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and deploy solutions in SaaS, hybrid cloud, and customer managed environments, with working familiarity across containers, Kubernetes, CI or CD, and infrastructure automation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define or refine dashboards, alerting, service boundaries, and reliability workflows so customer teams can operate what is deployed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner during go live, hypercare, and troubleshooting periods to drive adoption, reduce friction, and make the solution durable in production.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert repeated field learnings into templates, playbooks, reusable components, and product feedback for core engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt; color: rgb(126, 140, 141);&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, maintainable code across backend and frontend systems, commonly using Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, and React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement integrations with third-party systems using APIs and SDKs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing, debugging, and optimization of deployed solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow engineering best practices for reliability, security, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal documentation and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reusable artifacts created, such as templates, integration patterns, playbooks, or productized improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prototype &amp;amp; Iterate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop MVPs and proof-of-concept solutions to validate customer use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate feedback from customers and internal stakeholders to refine functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the transition of validated solutions into scalable product capabilities in collaboration with product and core engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer &amp;amp; Partner Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in technical discussions with customers and partners alongside senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide implementation support and troubleshooting during deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share insights and feedback from customer engagements with internal teams to improve product quality and usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production deployments launched and adopted by named customer teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time to first value, such as first workflow live, first integration live, or first meaningful AI investigation or automation in production.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurable workflow impact, such as reduced manual triage, faster incident handling, lower alert noise, or improved operational efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong implementation quality, documentation quality, and stakeholder satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-7 years of experience in backend or data systems engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building streaming data pipelines (Kafka / Spark or any similar technology).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming background in Java and Python, including microservice design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ETL, data modeling, and distributed storage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to ship clean, production quality code in Java or Python plus JavaScript or TypeScript, whether gained in software engineering, platform engineering, solutions engineering, SRE, or technical consulting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to integrate external systems using APIs, SDKs, authentication controls, payload mapping, and schema validation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of observability fundamentals, including logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, alerting, root cause investigation, and incident workflows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with OpenTelemetry concepts and telemetry pipelines, including how data is instrumented, collected, and routed across systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of modern cloud and deployment tooling such as AWS, Azure, or GCP, containers, Kubernetes, CI or CD, and infrastructure automation tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical exposure to AI application patterns such as LLM APIs, agents or workflows, evaluation basics, and the observability of AI systems in production.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging judgment, systems thinking, and the ability to make progress in ambiguous customer environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of data governance, validation, and lineage best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration across AI, Data, and Platform teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain technical tradeoffs to engineers, product teams, and customer stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: ServiceNow or Jira workflows, automation tooling such as Ansible, Terraform, or Rundeck, and familiarity with MCP or similar integration patterns.&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(126, 140, 141);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
